{
  "step_1": "The decision reason can be applied to the decision problem. The reason focuses on the outcomes of each lottery, prioritizing losses over gains and specifically considering the maximum loss (i.e., the worst possible outcome) of each lottery. In Lottery A, the maximum loss is -6000 Euros; in Lottery B, the maximum loss is -3000 Euros. Since the reason emphasizes the more favorable (i.e., less severe) maximum loss, it would prefer Lottery B over Lottery A because -3000 Euros is better than -6000 Euros. The relevant information—maximum losses and the emphasis on losses—is available from the problem description.",
